6. DESIGN NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Running-plane-fit offset check coupling:
  The _accept_by_running_plane_fit offset check (L1212-1215) ties centroid
  distance to the dihedral angle: both scale with the height of the tilted
  vertex.  Test fixtures use a perpendicular distance of only 10 cm from the
  shared edge (0.1x the model extent) to keep centroid displacement small
  enough to pass the balanced tolerance while still discriminating at accurate.

  Formula for the bent-strip fixture:
    dot(n1, n2) = 0.1L / sqrt(h^2 + 0.01L^2)
    angle = arccos(dot)
    centroid dist = h/3  (running fit, cnt=1 -> seed normal)
    offset_tol = max(1e-6, 1e-4*extent) for balanced
    offset_tol = max(1e-8, 1e-6*extent) for accurate

