7. POST-REVIEW FIXES (2026-08-05)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bug A — analyze_mesh dead params:
  The analyze_mesh tool accepted the 5 new params in its signature but never
  forwarded them to analyze_mesh_data.  Fixed: the call now passes
  angle_tolerance_deg, offset_tol, snap_tol, simplify_vertices, preset.

Bug B — preset angle dead zone (None sentinel):
  With angle_tolerance_deg: float = 0.5 on analyze_mesh_data AND both MCP tools,
  the literal 0.5 was always forwarded to decompose, so preset angle overrides
  (e.g. preset="accurate" -> 0.1 deg) never activated through the tool path.
  Changed all three layers to Optional[float] = None, preserving baseline
  behavior (None -> decompose default 0.5) while allowing the preset's angle
  to take effect when angle is unspecified.

Regression tests added (tests/test_presets_tolerances.py):
  - test_analyze_mesh_data_preset_passthrough: preset="accurate" through
    analyze_mesh_data -> 2 faces (vs 1 for default, proves preset reaches
    decompose through the intermediate layer)
  - test_analyze_mesh_data_angle_override_wins: preset="coarse" + angle=0.05
    -> 2 faces (vs 1 for coarse alone, proves explicit float beats preset)

